-- title:
--   Crossings in the special fibre of X₀(Mp) are supersingular
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/p}$. Let $K_2 \subseteq L((q))$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, that is, the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the quotients $\mathrm{int}(p_f)/\mathrm{int}(p_g)$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ with $\mathrm{int}(p_g) \neq 0$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K_2$ compatible with $A \to L \to K_2$. Let $j \in K_2$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion $q^{-1}\,j_{\mathrm{num}}(q)$, the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), and let $B =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) $A\,K_2\,j$ be the subalgebra of elements of $K_2$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y \subseteq B$ be a prime ideal containing the image of $\varpi$, and suppose there are two distinct minimal primes $\mathfrak{p} \neq \mathfrak{p}'$ of the ideal $\varpi B$ with $\mathfrak{p} \le y$ and $\mathfrak{p}' \le y$. Then for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : B \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) $p\,\Omega$: every elliptic Weierstrass curve $W$ over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ satisfies $P = 0$ for every affine point $P$ of $W$ with $p \cdot P = 0$.
--
--   This is the classical assertion that the irreducible components of the special fibre of $X_0(Mp)$ in characteristic $p$ meet only at supersingular points, expressed in terms of prime ideals of the $j$-finite chart ring of the two-chart integral model of the function field of $X_0(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring. It feeds the analysis of which elements of the chart ring become nonunits, used in the level-lowering part of the argument.
